{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778531164272,"sessionID":"ses_1e74a060bffeVX9fS9YcXcrmgb","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-805660e6be58b0e6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json"},"output":"<path>/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"**Problems**\\n- In the current claude.md file, the agent is instructed to sign off as @dragon-ai-agent. \\n- The agent sometimes adds` AnnotationAssertion(dc:contributor obo:CL_0010000 \\\"dragon-ai-agent\\\") ` when updating the textual def of a term which:\\n1) fails the QC\\n2)In CL, we use `dcterms:contributor` only when creating a new term \\n\\n\\n**Changes**\\nUpdate claude.md - ie. \\n1) always sign your commits `GitHub Copilot`\\n2) Change ` created_by: dragon-ai-agent` to `dc:creator GitHub Copilot` and make it clear only to use this when creating new terms \\n\\n\\n**Another problem**\\n- Co-pilot only looks at CL ids in the cl-edit file when generating a new ID (so does not take into account Ids assigned in open PRs) - This has been fixed by Damien's implementation\\n\\n\\n\",\n3:   \"comments\": [],\n4:   \"title\": \"Update claude.md instructions for GitHub Copilot\",\n5:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3267\"\n6: }\n\n(End of file - total 6 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"**Problems**\\n- In the current claude.md file, the agent is instructed to sign off as @dragon-ai-agent. \\n- The agent sometimes adds` AnnotationAssertion(dc:contributor obo:CL_0010000 \\\"dragon-ai-agent\\\") ` when updating the textual def of a term which:\\n1) fails the QC\\n2)In CL, we use `dcterms:contributor` only when creating a new term \\n\\n\\n**Changes**\\nUpdate claude.md - ie. \\n1) always sign your commits `GitHub Copilot`\\n2) Change ` created_by: dragon-ai-agent